CVSS v3.1 Score
7.1 – High
CVSS Vector
CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:H/A:L
Description

The application restricts the Confirmation Agreed Timeout Interval field through a dropdown list in the user interface, allowing only predefined values such as:

15 Minutes
30 Minutes
45 Minutes
60 Minutes
90 Minutes
120 Minutes

However, during security testing it was identified that the application fails to enforce server-side validation for this parameter.

An authenticated user can intercept the HTTP request using Burp Suite and modify the interval parameter from an allowed value (e.g., 15) to an unauthorized value such as 500. The backend server accepts and processes the manipulated value successfully.

This demonstrates that validation is implemented only at the client-side level and can be bypassed through parameter tampering.

